 [{:title
   "Raw js/process.stdin access in infra.cli bypasses existing extern boundary",
   :file "packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/infra/cli/tui_repl.cljs",
   :detail
   "Line 123: `use-editor? (and (nil? get-input) (.-isTTY js/process.stdin))` touches a raw Node host object from `infra.cli.tui-repl`. This violates the constitution's extern rule (\"Nothing above `extern` touches a raw host object\") and the card's own DoD line \"No raw Node/terminal interop outside extern.*\". The boundary for exactly this already exists: `eta-mu.extern.process/stdin-tty?` (packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/extern/process.cljs:35-38) is `(boolean (.-isTTY js/process.stdin))`, and that namespace's docstring declares \"All direct access to `process` is isolated here.\" Fix is a one-line swap: require `[eta-mu.extern.process :as process]` and call `(process/stdin-tty?)`. Note sibling infra/cli/repl.cljs:71-156 has pre-existing raw js/process access, but that is legacy anomaly, not license for new violations in a card whose DoD explicitly forbids it.",
   :severity "blocker",
   :card "input-editor",
   :lens "architecture-law",
   :survives true,
   :reasons
   ["Verified against the actual code: packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/infra/cli/tui_repl.cljs line 140 contains exactly `use-editor? (and (nil? get-input) (.-isTTY js/process.stdin))` (the claim said line 123, but the quoted expression matches line 140 verbatim — a line-number slip, not a substantive error). git blame shows this line was introduced in commit 2732ca6 \"terminal-ui: raw-mode input editor\" — this card's own implementation commit, so it is not grandfathered code. The card's DoD (line 53) explicitly states \"No raw Node/terminal interop outside extern.*\" and that checkbox is unchecked; the constitution's namespace rule (\"Nothing above extern touches a raw host object\") independently forbids it. The correct boundary already exists: eta-mu.extern.process/stdin-tty? (extern/process.cljs:35-38) is literally `(boolean (.-isTTY js/process.stdin))` under a docstring declaring \"All direct access to `process` is isolated here.\" The card's comment history (decision record + implementation note) documents accepted tradeoffs for persistent history deferral and domain.fuzzy's caller, but never mentions or accepts this raw stdin access; the kanban ledger for the card shows only status changes and watcher drift events, no deferral record. The pre-existing raw access in infra/cli/repl.cljs:153-156 is indeed legacy (earlier commits) and is a logged anomaly, not authorization — the anomaly rule says anomalies are described, not propagated. The fix is a one-line swap to the existing extern fn. A violation of an explicit, card-authored DoD item, introduced by the card itself, is definitionally promotion-gating for a review→done move, so the blocker severity stands."
    "Claim verified on every material point. tui_repl.cljs line 140 (reviewer cited 123, off-by-line-number only; the quoted form is verbatim) contains `use-editor? (and (nil? get-input) (.-isTTY js/process.stdin))` — a raw Node host access from infra.cli. Git blame shows this exact expression was introduced by commit 2732ca6 'terminal-ui: raw-mode input editor', i.e. by THIS card's own implementation commit, so it is not grandfathered code. The boundary already exists in the same package: eta-mu.extern.process/stdin-tty? (extern/process.cljs:35-38) is exactly `(boolean (.-isTTY js/process.stdin))`, that ns docstring declares 'All direct access to `process` is isolated here', and a sibling infra namespace (infra/cli/commands/agent.cljs:100) already calls `(process/stdin-tty?)` for the same check — so the card's own codebase demonstrates the convention it violated. The card's DoD explicitly lists 'No raw Node/terminal interop outside extern.*', making this an unmet acceptance criterion, not a nitpick. Neither card comment (the persistent-history deferral nor the implementation summary) documents this raw access as an accepted tradeoff; the summary even claims the editor consumes keypresses 'via extern.terminal', so the stray process.stdin touch appears inadvertent. Fix is trivial (add the extern.process require, swap in stdin-tty?), which lowers cost but does not lower the gate: a finding that violates the card's own DoD, in code the card introduced, with an existing one-line boundary, is real, in-scope, and promotion-gating."]}
  {:title
   "Scope clause 'up/down across soft-wrapped input' is unimplemented and undeferrred — long lines desync the host row model",
   :file
   "packages/terminal-ui/src/cljs/eta_mu/terminal_ui/infra/input_editor.cljs",
   :detail
   "Card Scope lists 'Cursor movement: left/right/word-jump, home/end, up/down across soft-wrapped and multi-line input.' Only embedded-newline (hard) multi-line is delivered: editor-frame (input_editor.cljs:64-68) splits buffer text on \\n and never wraps at terminal width, while infra.host's contract (host.cljs docstring: frames are 'already wrapped/styled — this namespace doesn't wrap') requires pre-wrapped rows. Consequence: any input line longer than (terminal/columns term) occupies 2+ physical terminal rows but 1 frame row, so the host's :cursor-row bookkeeping and render-cursor!'s up-delta math (input_editor.cljs:70-80, computed in frame rows) drift from physical rows — subsequent diff renders repaint wrong rows and the cursor lands wrong. eb/move-line also cannot traverse visual rows of a soft-wrapped logical line. No test exercises a buffer line wider than the fake terminal's 80 columns, and no deferral of soft-wrap is recorded on the card (the recorded deferral covers only persistent history). All six DoD checkboxes pass regardless; maintainer should either fix or explicitly defer soft-wrap before review→done.",
   :severity "should-fix",
   :card "input-editor",
   :lens "dod-coverage",
   :survives true,
   :reasons
   ["Every factual element of the claim verifies against the code and card. (1) editor-frame (input_editor.cljs:64-68) splits buffer text on \\n and performs no width wrapping; input_editor.cljs never calls terminal/columns. (2) infra.host's docstring (host.cljs:5-6) states frames must be 'already wrapped/styled — this namespace doesn't wrap', and host/render! + extern.terminal/move-by (CSI A/B relative escapes) do all cursor math in frame-row units, so a logical input line longer than the terminal width soft-wraps onto 2+ physical rows while the host's :cursor-row and render-cursor!'s up-delta (input_editor.cljs:70-80) count 1 frame row — subsequent diff renders and cursor placement physically desync. Mechanism confirmed, not hypothetical. (3) The gap is squarely in scope: the card's Scope bullet explicitly lists 'up/down across soft-wrapped and multi-line input' — the delivered editor wires up/down to history-prev/history-next (escape-sequences, input_editor.cljs:29-30) and no key invokes eb/move-line at all, so even hard multi-line up/down cursor movement is undelivered; the claim actually understates the gap. (4) Not deliberate/documented: the card's two appended notes record only the persistent-history deferral and the fuzzy-caller note; the kanban ledger contains zero comment events for this card, and a repo-wide search shows 'soft-wrap' appears nowhere except the scope clause itself. (5) Not grandfathered: input_editor.cljs is new code delivered by this card. (6) Not minor: rendering corruption on any over-width input in the card's flagship deliverable, plus an explicitly scoped feature gap that all six DoD checkboxes are too weak to catch (they only demand domain-level tests, which pass via edit_buffer_test.cljs while no infra test feeds a line wider than the fake terminal's 80 columns — verified: longest test input is 7 chars). A fix-or-explicitly-defer decision before review→done is warranted; finding stands."
    "Every factual element of the claim verifies against the code and card. (1) Card Scope (terminal-ui-input-editor.md:35-36) explicitly lists 'up/down across soft-wrapped and multi-line input'. (2) editor-frame (input_editor.cljs:64-68) splits buffer text only on \\n and never wraps at terminal width — the editor never even calls terminal/columns, so it has no width awareness. (3) infra.host's docstring (host.cljs:5-6) does state frames must be 'already wrapped/styled — this namespace doesn't wrap', confirming the contract mismatch. (4) The desync mechanics are real: host/render! (host.cljs:42-53) does move-by arithmetic assuming 1 frame row = 1 physical row, and writing a row longer than the terminal width auto-wraps the physical cursor, corrupting :cursor-row bookkeeping so subsequent diff renders repaint wrong rows; render-cursor! (input_editor.cljs:70-80) computes its up-delta in frame rows and emits CUF (\\u001b[nC) which clamps at the right margin without wrapping, so for any buffer line wider than the terminal the cursor lands on the wrong physical row. (5) extern/terminal move-by/write have no wrap compensation. (6) No test exercises a line wider than the fake terminal's 80 columns (longest inputs are 'hello', 'ab\\ncd'). (7) The card's comment history records only the persistent-history deferral; the ledger and all other kanban cards contain no soft-wrap deferral or follow-on. Refutation grounds all fail: not factually wrong, not documented as deliberate, in-scope per the card's own Scope clause, introduced by this card's own commit (2732ca6), and not minor — cursor misplacement and repaint corruption on long pasted input is a user-visible defect in the card's core deliverable, and the finding only asks for a fix or an explicit recorded deferral before review→done."]}],
 :all
